Denis,

Here are some logs.

This is on an aarch64 machine running Arch Linux. Kernel 5.4.70, iwd 1.9
and connman 1.38. The wifi driver is brcmfmac. The driver firmware is:
Firmware: BCM4345/6 wl0: Sep 18 2020 02:27:58 version 7.45.221 (3a6d3a0 CY)
FWID 01-bbd9282b

These logs contain an SSID off/on and a reconnect event (as desired) then
followed immediately with an SSID off/on and a no-reconnect event. I
grabbed the journal log from iwd and connman and also the pcap in case
any/all may be useful. I was able to see content that scrolled by on the
screen in the pcap with 'iwmon -F 0x17 -r no_reconnect.pcap' (I think you
mentioned this previously).

On a separate note, I was able to build and install iwd 1.9 for the RasPiOS
image. When running there, iwd 1.9 works as advertised with the same
performance as iwd 0.14. Reconnects almost immediately every time. Still
trying to update connman to 1.38 for the RasPiOS image.

Thanks for the help.

Keith


